WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.220
- [Lorenzo] Mental health
in the Black community

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:04.503
has been a problem for decades.

00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.270
A lot of that plays into the
stigma about mental health

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.600
and the reason why people are not going

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.250
to get the help that's necessary.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.510
Barbershops are a safe place
for young men of color.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:19.400
Barbers are our only people in our lives

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.200
that we allow to get close
proximity with a razor.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.440
We realize the barber become our friends,

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.730
and that's really important
because I could've used

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.460
that same space and work with barbers

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.274
to talk about our mental health.

00:00:30.274 --> 00:00:33.357
(gentle piano music)

00:00:35.965 --> 00:00:38.400
(gentle string music)

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.720
My name is Lorenzo Lewis,

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:43.550
and I am the founder and
CEO of The Confess Project.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:46.130
The Confess Project is a
national grassroots movement

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:48.070
that is geared around building a dialogue

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:50.800
of mental health for young men of color.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.560
I had a lot of problems as a young person.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.210
My mother was incarcerated when
I was born into this world,

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:58.240
and with losing my dad at the age of 10,

00:00:58.240 --> 00:00:59.940
I didn't know how to deal with it.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:04.150
I would go to this beauty
salon everyday after school,

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:05.510
and there was a barber there,

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:08.020
and I never forget a lot of the nurturing

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:09.330
and care that I got from him

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.130
really empowered me to wanna do better,

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:14.340
really wanted to empower
me to do good in school.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.090
I realized that I'm not
the only one struggling.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:19.080
Suicide is the third
leading cause of death

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:22.270
for young men of color
between the ages of 18 and 24.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:23.910
And a lot of this plays into communities

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:26.710
where there are a lot of
violence and toxic masculinity.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:30.340
So the barbershop was a perfect place

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:31.823
to start The Confess Project.

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:37.280
I walk into a barbershop and ask them

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.090
if I can have a moment of their time,

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:41.970
and then that moment turns
in an educational session.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.760
Thank you all for being here today.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:44.920
I think the most important part

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.720
of why I really came here today,

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:48.970
is to really so that I exhibit to you all

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:50.390
how we can break through our pain,

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:52.750
and how to part with
that being our purpose.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:55.810
Our goal is to not train barbers
to be mental health experts

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:57.890
but to train them to be
mental health advocates.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:59.350
We're training them with the skills

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:02.340
of active listening,
communication, validation,

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:05.410
to not be judgemental, to
be sensitive with language

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:07.450
so that their clients
can be able to open up

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:09.310
and possibly go and get some help

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.270
and treatment that may be necessary.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:14.500
- I've always been feeling
in a depressed state

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.950
and I never knew why.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:18.890
I still don't know why.

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:20.006
- To be completely honest,

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:22.020
it was the first time I've
ever heard a black man talk

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.830
about his struggles with mental health

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:27.050
or his emotions with
feeling like he's low,

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:29.340
feeling like he's in that
hole that he can't get out of.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.860
And that's a feeling that
I felt before growing up.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.020
It's a feeling that I felt often,

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:34.180
and it's a feeling that I was feeling

00:02:34.180 --> 00:02:36.630
in that time that I came to here.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.210
- I thought it was very powerful,

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:40.050
seeing black men coming together,

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.740
hugging and sharing that
valuable moment together.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.300
And you could see it in their eyes

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:47.942
and in their emotion.
(crowd applauding)

00:02:47.942 --> 00:02:51.220
(calm instrumental music)

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.720
- Since starting The Confess Project,

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.140
we have now expanded to nine U.S. cities

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.470
across the southern and mid-west region.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:02:59.460
It's really important to
keep that momentum going,

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:02.010
and we realize that we still
have a lot of work to do.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:04.950
And it's one of those things
where we have to create leaders

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.760
and build a generation of leaders,

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:09.250
so that they can be
sustained and also go out

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:10.770
and help many more community members

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:12.590
that we may not reach.

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:15.360
What I specifically love about my job is

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.460
that I get to work with that side of me

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:19.770
that I wasn't able to
get that same help with

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:22.760
and help young men of
color to really thrive

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.332
and to really become the
best version of who they are.

00:03:26.332 --> 00:03:29.499
(gentle string music)

00:03:30.686 --> 00:03:33.436
(gentle ringing)

